              `A high-converting cold email is short (under 100 words is ideal), specific to the individual recipient, and makes the reader feel that ignoring it costs them something. The subject line has one job: earn the open. The opening line has one job: earn the second sentence. The value proposition has one job: make the reader curious. The CTA has one job: make responding easy.`,
              `The PASTOR framework is the most effective structure for cold email copywriting. It forces you to lead with the prospect's problem — not your product — and to make them feel understood before you make any ask. Personalisation is not just adding someone's first name. It means referencing something specific: a recent funding round, a LinkedIn post they wrote, a new hire they made, a technology they use. The prospect should feel like you wrote this email to them specifically.`
