              `The DESC model gives you a structure to enter difficult conversations with clarity and confidence. It prevents the two most common failure modes: being too vague (so the issue doesn't get resolved) and being too aggressive (so the relationship suffers). The model forces you to separate the description of the facts from your interpretation or reaction, which dramatically reduces defensiveness.`,
              `Delivering bad news early is always better than delivering it late. A prospect who discovers mid-implementation that the product has a key limitation you knew about is not just disappointed — they're betrayed. A prospect who hears the same information before signing, delivered clearly and with honesty, respects the transparency and adjusts their expectations. Trust is built in difficult moments, not easy ones.`
