              `The retail sales opening is the highest-leverage moment of the entire interaction. "Can I help you?" generates 70% "no, just looking" responses. It's a question designed to be deflected. The expert retail opener is either a genuine observation about what the customer is looking at ("I see you're looking at the walnut range — they just came in last week"), or an open question about their purpose ("What's the occasion?"). Both create conversation without pressure.`,
              `Needs assessment in retail is a rapid skill. Three targeted questions tell you almost everything: What are they looking for (category)? Who is it for (gift, personal)? What matters most to them (quality, price, style)? With these answers, you can guide them to the right product and frame it in terms of their specific priorities — rather than presenting generic features.`
