              `The mistake most new salespeople make is defaulting entirely to one end of this spectrum. Hyper-competitors who share nothing, hoard leads, and celebrate others' failures may hit their personal quota but create an environment that the best people leave — including eventually them. Hyper-collaborators who spend more time helping others than building their own pipeline never build the individual track record that earns promotions and financial reward.`,
              `The professional sweet spot is: compete hard on your own numbers, share what works, celebrate your colleagues' wins genuinely, and never engage in politics that require diminishing others. This approach creates internal champions — colleagues who have experienced your generosity and will reciprocate in ways that you can't anticipate in advance.`
