              `This module builds on the basic BRIEF framework from Breaking Into Sales by adding advanced techniques for handling the most common cold call objections, navigating different prospect personalities, and creating micro-commitments throughout the call that lead naturally to a meeting booking.`,
              `The permission-based opening is a structural improvement to any cold call script. Rather than launching into a pitch the moment someone picks up, you first confirm they have 30 seconds and are willing to hear your reason for calling. This small act of respect for their time dramatically reduces defensiveness and increases the percentage of calls that remain conversations. It also immediately differentiates you from the 99% of callers who just launch.`,
              `The three most common cold call objections — and their expert responses — must be rehearsed to the point of automatic reflex. These are: "I'm not interested," "Send me an email," and "We're already using something for that." Each objection has a specific response architecture that acknowledges the resistance without surrendering the conversation. The unprepared rep either pushes through awkwardly or caves immediately. The prepared rep acknowledges, reframes, and asks one targeted question.`
