              `Research by Salesloft and Outreach (leading sales engagement platforms) consistently shows that prospects contacted via 3+ channels convert at 2–3x the rate of those contacted via a single channel. This is not surprising — people use different channels with different levels of attention. A prospect who ignores three emails might respond immediately to a LinkedIn voice note. A prospect who doesn't answer calls might reply to a carefully crafted email on day 14 of a cadence.`,
              `The most effective cadence structure interleaves channels without being aggressive: call on day 1, email on day 1 (leave a voicemail if no answer), LinkedIn connection request on day 3, email on day 5, call on day 7, LinkedIn message on day 10, email on day 14, call on day 18, final email on day 28. This creates 10 touchpoints over 28 days — enough to be persistent without being offensive.`,
              `Personalisation within a cadence does not require individually writing every email from scratch. A well-designed cadence has a personalised Email 1 (fully individual-specific), semi-personalised Emails 2 and 3 (company-level personalisation with templates), and templated Emails 4 and 5 (designed to work across your whole ICP). The personalisation investment should be front-loaded — in the touchpoints most likely to generate a first response.`
