              `The expert voicemail is 15–20 seconds long, mentions the prospect's specific company by name, references one specific relevant observation, states your value prop in one sentence, gives your callback number slowly and clearly — twice — and ends. That's it. The goal is not to sell on the voicemail. The goal is to generate enough curiosity that the prospect either calls back or is receptive to the email you send immediately after.`,
              `The double-tap strategy is the most effective voicemail technique available. Leave the voicemail, then immediately send an email with the subject line: "[Name] — voicemail." The email says: "Just left you a voicemail — easier to read than listen. Here's what I said: [3-sentence email version]." This way, even if they delete the voicemail without listening, they see the email. And if they listen to the voicemail and read the email, you've created two touchpoints in one action.`
