              `This is why champion development is the single most important activity in a complex sale. A prospect contact who likes your product but has no access to the economic buyer cannot close the deal. A prospect contact who has economic buyer access but doesn't personally believe in the value won't make the case. Your champion needs: access (they can get in front of the decision-maker), credibility (the decision-maker trusts their judgment), and motivation (they personally benefit from the problem being solved).`,
              `Qualifying a champion requires testing their willingness to act — not just their stated enthusiasm. The champion test involves making specific, escalating requests: "Can you share the proposal internally?" "Can you arrange 20 minutes with the CFO?" "Can you tell me what happens in the internal review and where we might face resistance?" A true champion does these things. A friendly contact gives you warm words and no action.`
