              `The core AE operating model is built on one principle: pipeline coverage. Most AEs need 3–4x their quota in active pipeline to reliably hit 100% attainment — because deals slip, stall, and die. An AE with a £500K annual quota needs £1.5–2M in active, progressing pipeline at any given time. Managing this pipeline is not passive — it requires constant assessment of deal health, proactive action on at-risk deals, and consistent prospecting to replace deals that fall out.`,
              `Time allocation is the most critical operating decision an AE makes every week. The default trap: spending 80% of time on late-stage deals (exciting, close to revenue) and 20% on pipeline building (boring, long-term). The correct model: protect at least 25–30% of each week for prospecting and pipeline generation, regardless of current pipeline health.`
