              `The most important insight about procurement: they almost always have a preferred vendor by the time the formal process begins. The structured evaluation, scoring matrix, and competitive bidding process is often compliance theatre designed to satisfy internal policies while reaching a decision that was effectively made before the RFP was issued. Understanding this means that winning procurement processes requires winning the relationships with the actual buyers before procurement gets involved.`,
              `The AE who enters a procurement process without having already built a relationship with the technical buyer, the business owner, and ideally a senior sponsor is playing a price game — competing on a scorecard against vendors the real buyers don't prefer. The AE who is the incumbent favourite — having already won the internal recommendation — uses procurement to confirm and structure the commercial relationship, not to compete for it.`
