              `The SE role is uniquely positioned at the intersection of sales and engineering. An exceptional SE has the business empathy of a salesperson (can translate technical capability into business value) and the technical credibility of an engineer (can answer architecture questions, discuss API design, explain data models, and engage in security reviews). This combination is rare — and in B2B SaaS, increasingly valuable.`,
              `The SE and AE must operate as a team with clear division of responsibility. The AE manages the commercial relationship, business stakeholders, and deal timeline. The SE manages the technical relationship, evaluates technical fit, and designs the technical solution. Confusion about these roles — either AE trying to handle technical questions they can't answer credibly, or SE getting involved in commercial discussions that aren't their domain — is a common source of enterprise deal failure.`
