              `The most common security review elements: SOC 2 Type II report (reviewed by the customer's InfoSec team), pen test results (evidence of independent third-party security testing), DPA / data processing agreement (required for any vendor handling personal data under GDPR), vendor security questionnaire (often 100–200 questions covering all security domains), and sometimes a CISO-to-CISO conversation for the most sensitive deals.`,
              `The SE's role in security reviews: compile and maintain a security pack (all standard security documentation ready to send), respond to vendor questionnaires with accurate, documented answers, engage the customer's InfoSec team directly if needed, and act as the conduit between the customer's technical concerns and your company's security team.`
