              `The test for SaaS pricing is always: does the value we deliver justify the price we charge? If your product saves a customer £50,000 per year in efficiency and you charge £5,000 per year, you are dramatically underpriced. A 10:1 value-to-price ratio gives the customer a clear ROI story. A 100:1 ratio (£500 per year for £50,000 of value) leaves enormous value on the table and signals to sophisticated buyers that the product may not be as good as it claims (because price signals quality).`,
              `Discovering the right price requires testing: asking potential customers what they pay for comparable solutions, what they'd pay for your solution, and what would feel like "too cheap to be trusted." The Goldilocks zone — not too cheap to be credible, not too expensive to justify — is identifiable through systematic pricing research before you price-lock.`
