              `Effective sales coaching is proactive, systematic, and behaviour-specific. It is scheduled (1:1 sessions every week), structured (consistent framework applied consistently), and specific (anchored in observable behaviours, not personality assessments). "You need to build more urgency" is not actionable coaching. "In the last three calls, you presented the pricing before asking about their decision timeline — let's look at what happens when you reverse that sequence" is actionable coaching.`,
              `The most effective coaching moments come from call recordings. A manager who reviews one call recording per rep per week and arrives at the 1:1 with three specific, behaviour-based observations is providing infinitely more valuable coaching than the manager who asks "so how's it going?" The specificity of "at minute 12 you said X, and the prospect's response was Y — what could you have said instead?" is the difference between development that sticks and feedback that evaporates.`
