              `Deal strategy must be explicit and written. An AE running a £500K deal "in their head" will miss variables, miss stakeholders, and miss timing signals that a written deal plan captures. The deal plan forces honesty: do I actually know the decision process? Have I met the economic buyer? Is my champion strong enough to win internally? These questions, written down, reveal gaps that can still be closed. Unwritten, they are comfortably unexamined.`,
              `The most common large deal failures: single-threading (the entire relationship rests on one champion who leaves or loses influence), no compelling event (the deal has no urgency and drifts indefinitely), invisible competition (a competitor is preferred by a stakeholder you haven't engaged), and paper-close-date syndrome (the AE's forecast shows the deal closing next month, and has shown the same for 4 months).`
