              `Commercial legacy is built by three types of contribution: the outcomes you delivered (revenue generated, customers acquired, teams built), the people you developed (reps you coached, managers you mentored, careers you influenced), and the standards you set (the level of integrity, professionalism, and excellence you modelled throughout your career). The first is visible in your CV. The second and third are visible in the network, reputation, and professional relationships you carry throughout your career.`,
              `The commercial professionals who are most sought out, most referred, and most valued at every stage of their careers are almost universally the ones who are known for: excellence in their craft (they were consistently good), integrity in their dealings (they could be trusted), and generosity with their knowledge and time (they made others better). These three characteristics, compounded across a career, produce something that cannot be manufactured in a single year of high performance: a professional reputation that precedes you everywhere you go.`,
              `The meta-lesson of SalesLab: selling is not a transactional activity you do to buyers. It is a professional discipline — as demanding and as rewarding as any other. The professional who masters it, who combines commercial skill with genuine integrity and authentic care for their customers' success, builds a career that is by any measure exceptional: financially rewarding, intellectually engaging, and deeply meaningful in its impact on the organisations and people they serve.`
